WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.269 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  i grew up on a farm in egypt  being the creative genius that i was i  named our cows  chicken and sheep after family and  friends the uglier the animal the more  likely they would be named after one of  my sisters  i remember one particularly adorable cow  that we got when i was six so i named it  after my best friend at the time  ali a couple of months into  his arrival onto our farm i watched  ali get slaughtered a horrible  experience that i wish  upon no one's best friend's namesake  understandably i skipped meat for dinner  that night  and the following and the following and  the following  until one day my mother was fed up  she snapped at me at the dinner table  and said  you ate burger yesterday why are you not  eating the steak that i just cooked for  you  i stared at my steak then back at my mom  i asked her is burger cow too  to her dismay her efforts to get me to  eat meat that night  backfired i never ate a burger again now  that i knew what it was made of  but six-year-old me is not that  different from many of us  hardly any of the adults i know know how  their food makes it to their table  luckily for my parents by the time i was  13 i'd  reconciled myself with the fact that  humans do kill mammals for food  my parents started making me eat more  red meat  but something still didn't feel quite  right  so being the nerd that i was still am  honestly  i started researching human's  relationship  with food once again  my mother's efforts to get me to eat  meat backfired  after learning about the food industry i  decided to go  plant-based plant-based meant that  i was not eating not only red meat but  any animal product  being plant-based in egypt a country  where one of the biggest religious  celebrations  includes the slaughter of a mammal and  distributing its  meat to charity was the equivalent of  being a pagan  in fact my mom's efforts backfired big  time  this time i managed to make my whole  family  go plant-based unfortunately  it was not due to my masterful rhetoric  it was simply my mother's solution to  not cook  two meals one without animal products  for me  and one with for the rest of the family  but over the first year of going  plant-based as a family we started  noticing something  interesting my mother started  losing weight making her way out of  obesity and my father  reversed his hypertension  but my parents were not doing something  new here  they were simply adopting the diet of  our ancestors  when they didn't have access to a  carcass 24 7  in their fridge but simply roamed around  earth eating plants nuts  and a small animal every once in a while  so why do i have beef with the meat  industry  well six-year-old me had an issue with  the beef part of the phrase  but adult me has an issue with the  industry part of the phrase  all parties are losing it's a horrible  system  the workers are losing the animals are  losing our health is losing  and the planet is losing well  all parties accept the corporations four  of which  control eighty percent of the industry  me today is half as cheap as it used to  be a hundred years ago adjusted for  inflation  and for me to be this cheap someone had  to pay the price along the value chain  the workers pay the price nothing slows  down  the production line not animal  excrements not exhausted workers  not injured hands in some  slaughterhouses not even  the workers urged to use the bathroom  they urinate  and defecate on the production line lest  they slow down a system  that expects them to kill 35 to 45  chickens per minute do the math  that's less that's less than two seconds  per bird  they do this all day long for every  working day of their lives only to be  paid  500 a week pre-tax  it's not a surprise that the animals pay  the price  if you're a cow in america this is what  your life looks like you are  raised on a concrete slab in a stall  barely big enough for your own body  you never touch the grass or see the  sunlight until the day you're hurt to  slaughter  you are fed corn because it's cheap and  it makes you fat  fast even though you did not evolve to  eat it your hooves have rotten black  from standing in your own poop all day  your tail has been cut without  anesthesia to stop hitting the workers  and a cocktail of hormones and some  breathing decisions  is making you grow at unprecedented  rates that your own bones cannot carry  you  but hey you need to grow fast to keep up  with the demand  the average american consumes the  equivalent of  1.5 steaks per day in the form of  chicken  fish bacon any form of meat  this might not seem like a lot to you  except that the world health  organization  indicates that the consumption of  anything more than 50 grams  or the equivalent of a quarter of a  steak  1 6 of what we consume triggers the  onset of cancer  and cardiovascular diseases among many  many others  british research on over 11 000 people  shows that vegetarians are 40 percent  less likely to get cancer and that  vegetarian women  live on average six years longer and  vegetarian men  10 years longer than their meat eating  counterparts  we're literally paying the price in days  of our lives  i have so much beef with the meat  industry because  even though i choose not to eat meat i  am still paying the price  our planet is suffering  cow farts are suffocating us and  men do cows fart a lot  15 of the greenhouse gases are  attributed  to the meat industry the industry is  taking a huge toll on our  resources do you know what's you  eating drinking showering cleaning for  six months  have in common with one kilogram of beef  you both consume the same amount of  water  it's an incredibly wasteful system it's  an incredibly expensive  system so as a plant-based eater  here is what i ask you enjoy  your meat make it a delicacy  not a daily thing eat it once or twice a  week  then once or twice a month and if i'm  doing my job here  a few times a year  don't listen to me educate yourself  watch literally any food documentary  watch john oliver's episode  on meat packing and then make the  decision for yourself  see if you still feel good consuming  certain products  finally invite your friends have vegan  dinners  have vegetarian mondays make it a group  activity  so enjoy your meat  don't listen to me educate yourself and  invite  your friends  wow six-year-old me  was such a visionary  you

